menu "OLED Display Settings"

    config OLED_PIN_SDA
        int "OLED SDA Pin"
        default 17
        help
            GPIO pin number for the OLED display's dedicated I2C SDA line.
            This bus is separate from the shared I2C Manager bus.

    config OLED_PIN_SCL
        int "OLED SCL Pin"
        default 18
        help
            GPIO pin number for the OLED display's dedicated I2C SCL line.
            This bus is separate from the shared I2C Manager bus.

    config OLED_PIN_RESET
        int "OLED Reset Pin"
        default 21
        help
            GPIO pin wired to the OLED's hardware reset line (RST_OLED on
            Heltec WiFi LoRa32 V3 boards). Without toggling this pin the panel
            never leaves reset and silently fails to ACK on the I2C bus.
            Set to -1 if the display has no dedicated reset pin.

    config OLED_PIN_VEXT
        int "OLED Vext (power enable) Pin"
        default 36
        help
            GPIO pin controlling the Vext power rail that feeds the OLED on
            Heltec boards. Driven LOW to switch the rail on. Without this the
            display has no power at all. Set to -1 if the board has no Vext
            switch (display is always powered).

    config OLED_REQUIRE_UNSCII_8_FONT
        bool
        default y
        select LV_FONT_UNSCII_8
        help
            Forces LVGL's unscii_8 bitmap font on. Anti-aliased fonts (e.g. the
            default Montserrat) render almost invisibly on 1bpp displays,
            since LVGL's I1 blend only lights a pixel at 100% coverage; a
            crisp, non-anti-aliased bitmap font is needed instead.

endmenu